                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I don't even know what to add what other reviewers have also said. This game is a Frankenstein's monster of puzzle/rhythm game, with none of the benefits. The game has elements of Tetris, Lumines for the puzzle side. Rhythm side you match the beat, similar to DDR, Parappa the Rapper, etc,\n\nThe big issue I have with this game, is that all the elements and design of this game just doesn't work. It forces you to match the pace of the music, but also asking you to manage and control things like in Lumines. this makes it where you have to slow your damn brain down to the music, but your mind also is trying to match puzzle pieces. It's literally a cognitive dissonance of gameplay. You wan to go fast to match tiles, but are forced to wait for the beatline to allow you to match. \n\nThe music isn't helping either. Several songs in and I just can't care any less over the music direction for it. If this is some musical journey, I rather stay at home. I can't even summarize beyond some mix of EDM and a guitarist that is high on ketamine. Nothing about the music is memorable, and makes me feel like I'm playing a bargain bin Nintendo DS game.\n\nI love puzzle games, and rhythm games, this abomination is a clear warning that some mechanics can not, and should not, be mixed together.",
